Reverted by known_bugs.sh to reintroduce the bug fixed by dd59355d4:
voice core: what the deep seeds found. AMD's own recognition stream, opened while the detector 
closed, queued on its channel and dropped with it, is closed (amd_tap_queued_at_close, survey 
seed 7022); a reply created behind a speech that goes on to a tool step is planned once that step 
is recorded with its tools, not at the speech's end: it held the floor the tool step needed, and 
both waited out the replan's six-second bound (reply_behind_tool_step, survey seed 14338)

diff --git a/rust/crates/lk-agents-voice/src/amd/detector.rs b/rust/crates/lk-agents-voice/src/amd/detector.rs
index 587eb91de..4432fbba8 100644
--- a/rust/crates/lk-agents-voice/src/amd/detector.rs
+++ b/rust/crates/lk-agents-voice/src/amd/detector.rs
@@ -309,6 +309,15 @@ impl AmdSystem {
                 () = api.closed() => break,
             }
         }
+        // A tap that opened while the system was closing is still queued here: dropped with the
+        // channel it would never be closed, and a dropped host stream is never cancelled.
+        msgs.close();
+        while let Ok(msg) = msgs.try_recv() {
+            if let Msg::SttOpened(Ok((_sink, source))) = msg {
+                self.peer.journal(Step::Input(InputStep::LegOpenDiscarded { leg: TAP }));
+                self.discard_tap(source);
+            }
+        }
     }
 
     /// One item off the feed: what the reference's `AudioRecognition` hands the classifier.
diff --git a/rust/crates/lk-agents-voice/src/generation/pipeline_reply.rs b/rust/crates/lk-agents-voice/src/generation/pipeline_reply.rs
